  "source_scope": {
    "input": "The same public cached floor-curve descriptors, both original orientations, and the actual positive denominators 1<=t<m. No factors or local orders enter the constructors.",
    "generic_polynomial_scope": "Every commutative ring with unit A,B, 0<u<m and gcd(m,u)=1; a coefficient domain is not required for monic polynomial cancellation.",
    "actual_public_premises": "For 1<m, gcd(m,N)=1 and gcd(j,m)=1, the original representative u_j is positive, less than m and coprime to m. The public descriptor obeys the exact Euclidean relation; m need not be prime.",
    "field_projection_scope": "The zero-disjunction theorem is over a field. It preserves a shifted-parent alternative and does not claim that child roots alone capture every parent root.",
    "obstruction_scope": "Generic retained floor curves at u=1, orientation false, 1<t<m and m<orderOf A. This is a uniform structural theorem conditional on a public step of sufficient order; it is not a new exhaustive semiprime miss or a proof that every actual public source/base contains such a target.",
    "unchanged_prior_scope": "The old scalar/two-axis complete miss, loop-only complete miss, dense balanced arithmetic forcing, carry-index transport and boundary input/count bounds are unchanged."
  },
  "exact_arithmetic": {
    "jump_level_index": "t_k=floor((m*k-1)/u), for 1<=k<=u. The map is a bijection onto the complete original jumpSet, with after-floor k and before-floor k-1.",
    "last_level": "t_u=m-1, so the final after-jump root is the original F_m endpoint.",
    "interior_level": "For 0<k<u and gcd(m,u)=1, t_k+1=floor(m/u)*k+floor((m mod u)*k/u)+1, retaining the exact ceiling offset.",
    "child_parameters": "q=floor(m/u), r=m mod u, A_child=A^q*B^(-1), B_child=A^(-1), child modulus u, child slope r, canonical child orientation false.",
    "orientation_phase": "alpha=A*B^(-epsilon)=F_1, where epsilon is the original parent orientation.",
    "interior_after_root": "F_(t_k+1)=alpha*F_child(k), exactly for 1<=k<u.",
    "interior_before_root": "A*F_(t_k)=(alpha*B)*F_child(k), exactly for 1<=k<u.",
    "phased_child": "Q_S(X)=S^(u-1)*P_child(X/S), retaining every child root with multiplicity. This is a mathematical product/substitution definition.",
    "complete_after_boundary": "J_plus(X)=(X-F_m)*Q_alpha(X).",
    "complete_before_boundary": "J_minus(X)=(X-B*F_m)*Q_(alpha*B)(X).",
    "monic_endpoint_cancellation": "The common polynomial X-F_m is regular because it is monic. It is cancelled at the polynomial source over every commutative coefficient ring; no unit or nonzero premise about x-F_m is imposed.",
    "exact_target_relation": "A^(m-1)*P(X/A)*Q_alpha(X)*(X-alpha)=P(X)*(X-B*F_m)*Q_(alpha*B)(X).",
    "coprime_descent": "gcd(u,m mod u)=1 follows from gcd(m,u)=1. The remainder is the ordinary Euclidean remainder; no fast whole-source acquisition or recursion-cost theorem follows from this fact.",
    "field_collision_transport": "If P(x)=0 then P(x/A)=0 or Q_alpha(x)=0 or x=alpha. This is a zero-preserving disjunction that retains the shifted parent.",
    "geometric_branch": "At u=1, Q_S=1 for every S. For 1<t<m and m<orderOf A, P(A^t)=0 while Q_alpha(A^t)=Q_(alpha*B)(A^t)=1, A^t differs from alpha=A and from B*F_m=A^m."
  },
